This repository contains a simple Java monorepo with multiple Spring Boot microservices. New services can be added under their own directories and referenced in the root `pom.xml`.

## Structure

- `service-a` – Sample microservice exposing `Hello from Service A`.
- `service-b` – Sample microservice exposing `Hello from Service B`.
- `scripts/buildChanged.sh` – Helper script to build and deploy only the services that changed between commits.
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` – GitHub Actions workflow using the script.

## Adding a New Service

1. Create a new module directory, e.g. `service-c` with its own `pom.xml` and source files.
2. Add the module name to the `<modules>` section of the root `pom.xml`.
3. The CI workflow will automatically build and deploy it when changes are made within that module.

## Building Locally

To build only changed modules against the last commit:

```bash
bash scripts/buildChanged.sh HEAD~1
```

To build all modules:

```bash
mvn install
```"
