- Initial working skeleton",production_grade,"The project is an enterprise-ready, privacy-first AI-powered test generation platform designed for regulated environments, with a full backend, frontend, CI/CD integration, and support for multiple LLM backends. It is suitable for real-world use in banks, government, and healthcare organizations, indicating substantive software beyond a toy or research prototype.",9,"# 🚀 Testly – Offline AI-Powered Test Generation Platform

**Testly** is a privacy-first, enterprise-ready tool for automating Playwright E2E test creation using advanced local LLMs.

## Key Features

* **On-premise/Offline:** All AI inference runs locally—no data leaves your environment.
* **Pluggable LLM Backend:** Supports MLC-LLM (default), with future support for Ollama (multi-model) and Claude API (cloud mode).
* **Backend:** Java (Spring Boot or preferred framework).
* **Frontend:** Node.js (React or similar), clean dashboard for test management.
* **CI/CD:** Seamless integration with GitHub Actions for automated test generation and execution.

## Architecture Overview

* User describes a test scenario or uploads API spec via UI/CLI.
* Java backend calls MLC-LLM (local) to generate Playwright test scripts.
* Generated scripts are reviewed, approved, and run using Playwright.
* Results are displayed in the dashboard; all workflows can be automated via CI/CD.

## Component Breakdown

| Component                       | Role / Purpose                                                                                        | Where Testly Innovates                                                              |
| ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **1. Java Spring Boot app**     | Backend API—handles user requests, security, orchestration, storage, and business logic               | Testly “glues” everything together, logs all actions for compliance                 |
| **2. Frontend (React/Node.js)** | User-facing dashboard: submit scenarios, upload API specs, review/edit generated scripts, see results | Unified experience for all test workflows                                           |
| **3. Testly Core Logic**        | Orchestrates: receives prompt/specs, calls local LLM, parses and post-processes LLM output            | **AI-powered, private test generation** (bulk from specs, not just one-off prompts) |
| **4. LLM Engine**               | MLC-LLM (local), Ollama (local), or Claude API (cloud, demo-only) for generating test scripts         | **Pluggable, privacy-first LLM inference**                                          |
| **5. Playwright Runner**        | Executes generated E2E test scripts (browser automation), returns detailed results                    | Integrates with CI/CD, works offline/on-prem                                        |
| **6. Results/Reporting**        | Stores and presents test outcomes, summaries, logs, compliance/audit reports                          | Centralized, auditable dashboard                                                    |

## Hardware

* **No GPU required** for small/medium LLMs and pilot deployments—CPU is sufficient.
* **GPU optional** for larger models or high-concurrency use.

## Why Testly?

* Designed for regulated, privacy-sensitive, or air-gapped environments.
* Automates and accelerates end-to-end test authoring, with full control and auditability.
* Future-proof: Swap in any LLM backend (Ollama, Claude, MLC-LLM) as business needs evolve.
* Combines AI-driven test generation, privacy, bulk automation and auditing **entirely offline**.
* Ideal for banks, government and healthcare organizations that cannot risk cloud leaks.
* Centralizes and automates workflows that are manual, slow and risky today.
* Simple to deploy and integrate, making it a future‑proof solution.

> “Testly brings secure, offline, AI-powered test automation to enterprises that can’t use cloud-based tools. Built for flexibility, it supports pluggable LLMs and integrates seamlessly into existing CI/CD and DevOps workflows.”

---

# Testly – System Flow & Architecture

## 1. High-Level Flow (End-to-End)

```
[User (QA/Dev)]
      │
      ▼
[Web Dashboard / CLI]
      │
      ▼
[Java Backend API (Spring Boot)]
      │
      ├───> [LLM Engine (MLC-LLM, Ollama, or Claude API)]
      │         └── (local CPU or GPU; API/CLI call)
      │
      └───> [Playwright Test Runner]
      │         └── (Executes E2E browser tests)
      │
      ▼
[Results & Reports]
      │
      ▼
[User Dashboard / CI Pipeline / Notifications]
```

## 2. Step-by-Step Flow

1. **User logs in to Testly web dashboard or starts CLI.**
2. **User enters test scenario, attaches an API spec, or points to source code.**
3. **Java backend** processes request and sends prompt/context to **LLM Engine**:

   * **Default:** Local MLC-LLM (no data leaves org)
   * **Future:** Swap in Ollama (local, multi-model) or Claude (cloud API, SaaS mode)
4. **LLM generates Playwright test scripts** (TypeScript/Python/etc.).
5. **Backend saves and displays generated scripts** for user review.
6. **User approves or edits scripts via dashboard/CLI.**
7. **Test scripts are executed by Playwright** (locally or in CI).
8. **Backend collects results, summarizes errors, generates coverage/report.**
9. **User views results in dashboard, exports reports, or integrates with bug tracker/notifications.**
10. **(Optional) All steps can run automatically via CI/CD (GitHub Actions, Jenkins, etc.).**

## 3. Deployment Design

### A. SaaS Demo/Pilot (on Fly.io)

* All components (frontend, backend, LLM engine, Playwright runner) containerized and deployed to Fly.io.
* Users access Testly via public URL.
* LLM may run as a microservice (for performance).
* Data is ephemeral, for demo only (not for sensitive use).
